docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:4:Native interviews complete through `ralph_complete_interview`. The plugin displays the explanation, scope, criteria, branch, full resolved HEAD SHA and command revision/hash in a native question. The affirmative option explicitly authorizes PRD creation, issue planning and automatic implementation within that scope. After the actual matching human response, the full create-prd snapshot enters the same session so it can author a feature PRD without editing project code.
docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:9:- Completion derives session identity from the host and checks the run owner, attempt and active control state. Arguments cannot carry an approval. Native results must match request, revision, session and unique human message identity; commit/configuration changes prevent approval.
docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:10:- Repeated pending proposals report their recorded request. Accepted duplicates cannot replace the explanation or reopen approval. Rejection returns to grilling; changed scope revokes authorization and dependent artifacts and requires a newly displayed revision.
docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:11:- PRD instructions include all 15 source template sections, the approved explanation, draft directory and an explicit `ralph_complete_prd` finish instruction. Delivery intent and a stable host message ID are persisted before queueing an inbox prompt. Queue acknowledgement does not wait for another child turn; failed delivery can retry without another approval.
docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:12:- In the PRD stage, `ralph_write_planning_file` accepts only stage-relative `PRD.md` in `.ralph/features/<run-id>/prd-draft-<attempt>/`. It checks authorization and ownership, rejects symlink ancestors/targets and writes atomically. Root PRDs, source paths, traversal, absolute paths, other runs and accepted revisions are outside its boundary.
docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:13:- Interview/PRD sessions can observe repository files and ask native questions. Catalog filtering and execution checks deny generic shell, write/edit, delegation, code mode and review aliases. Only the PRD stage gains the scoped writer. Existing reviewer and administrative restrictions remain separate.
docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:15:- PRD completion requires the owning session/attempt and active authorization, full nonempty required sections, and the supplied explanation revision/hash reference. API Specification and Appendix are optional. Invalid drafts return actionable correctable outcomes without a planner. Traversal and symlink sources are rejected.
docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:17:- The fresh owner can write only `graph.json` and safe `issues/<number>-<slug>.md` files under `issues-draft-<attempt>`. The former owner cannot replace accepted PRD bytes. Generic writes, shell and delegation remain denied at execution. The full to-issues adaptation preserves exploration, vertical slices, concrete patterns/tasks/test guidance and local Markdown; it removes tracker setup and breakdown approval.
docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:24:- `src/planning/prd.ts`, `src/opencode/adapter.ts` — same-session prompt delivery intent/queue and refusal to dispatch native PRDs as new jobs.
docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:25:- `src/planning/artifact-writer.ts`, `src/plugin.ts` — scoped atomic writes, tool registration, catalog and execution boundaries.
docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:26:- `src/state/run-store.ts` — revision guards and invalidation of scope-dependent authorization/output.
docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:28:- `tests/integration/03-interview.test.ts` — fake-host native approval, same-session template, rejection, stale/foreign results, repeated calls, denied delivery retry, writer and permission boundaries in real temporary Git projects.
docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:29:- `tests/integration/04-planning.test.ts` — native completion, exact accepted bytes/context, duplicate calls, invalid drafts/owners, symlinks, planner permissions and lost creation/prompt/focus receipts in real temporary Git projects; historical graph regressions use the full issue template.
docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:32:- `src/opencode/bridge.ts`, `src/tui.ts`, `tests/integration/tui-input.test.ts` — issue-stage focus events and location-scoped duplicate navigation suppression.
docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md:42:Legacy JSON generators, graph approval handlers and chat transport have been removed. All feature command entrypoints use native stage services. Unsupported saved workflows cannot resume or migrate; their artifacts remain intact.
