Task 17 was already finished in an earlier iteration, so I made no changes this time. I ran every validation step in order, and all of them pass:

- `bun --version` → 1.4.3
- `bun run typecheck` and `bun run lint` → no errors
- The focused interview and planning tests (`03-interview` and `04-planning`) → 56 pass, 0 fail
- `bun run test:status` → 15 pass, 0 fail
- `bun run test` (the full mandatory suite) → 293 pass, 0 fail, 1 skipped. The skipped test is the browser smoke test in `12-functional-review`, which only runs when `RUN_AGENT_BROWSER_SMOKE=1` is set.

Each acceptance criterion has a test through the plugin's public tools in `tests/integration/03-interview.test.ts`, with more cases in `04-planning.test.ts`:

- **Wrong session:** a completion call from a session that doesn't own the interview is rejected with an ownership error, and no approval question opens.
- **What the approval shows:** the question includes the explanation, acceptance criteria, branch, full commit SHA and command revision. Its "yes" option says it authorizes everything through implementation. Approval only counts when it comes back from the native question, never from the agent's own tool arguments.
- **PRD instructions:** nothing from the create-prd template reaches the session before approval. Afterwards, one queued prompt goes to the same session with all 15 sections and an instruction to finish with `ralph_complete_prd`. Calling completion again reports the existing request rather than opening a second one.
- **Rejection or scope change:** either one cancels the old authorization and requires a new revision to be shown. Scope changes also take away the writing tool.
- **Writing the draft:** `ralph_write_planning_file` (in `src/planning/artifact-writer.ts`) only writes `.ralph/features/<run>/prd-draft-<attempt>/PRD.md`. Writes to project source files, `..` paths, absolute paths, other runs, or through symlinks in the file or any parent folder are refused. Shell, write, edit, task, code-mode and reviewer-read tools are denied before they run and are also hidden from the agent's tool list.
- **Docs:** `docs/wiki/features/feature-planning.md` describes this behavior and points to the code and tests.
